## Course-level checks

Each year has a mid-year check and a year-end check. Each is the Check session of the unit it follows, widened: the unit's own end-of-unit page and watched rehearsal (so the unit is checked there, not twice), plus one or two items sampled from the year's earlier units on new cases, in one 30-minute session; its Respond session is the unit's Respond session, reteaching the steps the sheet shows "not yet" across the unit and the sampled items. They sit after units 2 and 5 (grade 3), 9 and 11 (grade 4), 15 and 17 (grade 5), so none falls in a week with a core course-level check for that grade (grade 3: 9, 12, 14, 16, 20, 23, 25, 28, 30 to 32; grade 4: 8 to 10, 12, 16, 19, 21, 23, 27, 30 to 32; grade 5: 10, 11, 16, 17, 21, 22, 29 to 32; docs/courses/CALENDAR.md). Unit sheets are thrown away at the end of their unit (Evidence); a check's sheet is kept only until its respond session, then thrown away. The last unit of each year comes after the year-end check: it is sampled by its own end-of-unit assessment and again by the next year's mid-year check (unit 6 by grade 4's, unit 12 by grade 5's); grade 5's unit 18 hands on to grade 6's retrieval items. On the short path each check and its respond share one session, the shared Check and Respond of the unit before it.

