311: ## For the lead
312: 
313: 1. **Unit sizes.** Grade 3 follows q-fix-sel-1 exactly (four 11s, two 10s); the course-level checks are the Check and Respond of units 2 and 5, which the 30-minute session can hold. Grades 4 and 5 run 10, 10, 10, 11, 11, 12 and 10, 10, 10, 11, 12, 11 (STANDARD section 2's moved session) so their mid-year check lands in week 15, clear of core weeks 10, 11 and 16. Pick: accept; the K to 2 shape (11/8) was not needed here.
314: 2. **Grade 6 rows.** g6-sa-name-feelings and g6-rel-stand-up describe as new what grade 3 already teaches (the strength scale; a choice among upstander options): row changes in the writer's report.
315: 3. **AASL ids for SEL.** scripts/progression.py and scripts/frame.py reject AASL.V.D.1, V.D.2 and III.D.2 in sel.csv standard cells; validator support is needed before they move there.
316: 4. **Health 3 to 5 side.** (a) Its I-statement says "Please ___"; STANDARD section 7 and g3-rel-settle-disagreements say "I need ___". Pick: health takes "I need ___". (b) Its listening steps (look, wait, ask one question, say back) and the talk turn card (listen, say back, ask a question, add your idea): pick one card, the talk turn card's words. (c) Its refusal steps are "new in grade 4" with "a short reason or none"; SEL grade 3 unit 5 teaches a four-step refusal with a reason a year earlier. Pick: health grade 4 unit 12 opens with SEL's card as retrieval and keeps "a reason is optional" as its health addition. (d) Its goal-plan and SEL's four-step goal steps card: health names the card's rungs. Health's For the lead 5 pick (keep stop-think-choose and the decision steps, each naming the other) is taken.
317: 5. **PE and computer science.** PE grades 3 to 5's frame (written beside this one) has three Pending notes on this frame (its SEL seam lines 359, 361, 362; stale.py now fails them); they can now name SEL units 1, 4, 7, 10, 11, 13 and 16 (Cross-subject, Physical education). Computer science grade 5's frame is not written; it cites unit 17 for g5-team-project.
