429: ### 9. Social and emotional learning
430: 
431: Decided 2026-11-11: these stay separate courses, not strands inside other subjects. They may be smaller than
432: other courses by the nature of the subject (see the pass rule for what that means).
433: 
434: **Rests on.** The SEL registry's criteria paper (2020): design criteria read in full by the writer and the expert.
435: 
436: 1. [I] All five competency areas are covered.
437: 2. [I] There is a sequence for each grade, or clear guidance for running a band over several years. One lesson set
438:    for a whole band earns the registry's lower design rating.
439: 3. [I] It is for every student, in school hours.
440: 4. [I] Sequenced: activities connect and build.
441: 5. [I] Active: managing oneself and getting on with others are practised by doing, such as acting out a hard
442:    moment or rehearsing a calming habit. The other areas are practised by reflection or talk.
443: 6. [I] Focused and explicit: set time, and each lesson names its skill.
444: 7. [I] Guidance for the adult, and a way to carry the skill beyond the lesson.
445: 8. [O] The course page states that no study stands behind the course.
446: 9. [O] Each unit names one link to that grade's core courses (a discussion routine, a civics row) the teacher may
447:    use. A lean, not a strand. (Items 9 to 13 added 2026-11-16, Cory, Desk card q-later-sel-eld, from the deeper
448:    review in docs/courses/sel/STANDARD.md section 4.)
449: 10. [O] Each unit carries the skill past the session: a "carry it out" cue for the school day and a family activity
450:     in the family note. Community is optional.
451: 11. [O] The scope and sequence states sessions a year. A paper fidelity checklist for the teacher (did the session
452:     run as planned, what was cut) and the class record of skill checks; no ratings of individual children.
453: 12. [O] Equity within the promises: family notes in English and Spanish; student voice in class and school life;
454:     bias taught as noticing and checking one's own snap judgements on invented cases, never as blame of a group.
455: 13. [O] Each unit's teacher page opens with a short "before you teach" note: the skill as an adult uses it, and one
456:     thing to model. Not training, and not claimed as such.
457: 
458: **Fails if:** posters and discussion with no practice; two of five areas; a band taught the same way every year.
459: 
460: **Unsupported.** The registry tests evidence first. The bar for these courses is the design half; the evidence half
461: is stated as unmet on the course page. Decided 2026-11-11: the design half is the bar; the deeper review was done 2026-11-16
462: (docs/courses/sel/STANDARD.md section 4).
463: 
464: **Standards.** data/standards/casel-5.txt, the same framework.
465: 
466: **Scope and sequence states:** the year-by-year sequence. **Section plan fills:** the practice by doing.
467: **Confidence:** likely for design.
