rengths hunt card, the private log, stop-think-choose, task cards. Curio Class writes the model webs, the case, the log page and the family note. Provisional cost for 30: about $9 printing. Begun here, owned in grade 5 (the band's owner year; the grade 5 unit that owns each is in the Seams table): CASEL.Self-Awareness.1, CASEL.Self-Awareness.2, CASEL.Self-Awareness.4, CASEL.Self-Awareness.9, CASEL.Social Awareness.2. | After unit 1 because the honest choice uses the four-step stop-think-choose; before unit 3 because a student names their own groups and strengths before reading others'. Five sub-skills, mostly reflection and talk, so two groups and 10 sessions, its Check and Respond being the mid-year check. Social studies grade 3 unit 7 (biographies, course days 141 to 160) comes later in the year (Cross-subject). Sessions 12 to 19 of the year, weeks 6 to 10; the mid-year check is sessions 20 and 21. | Candidate: the two-week log's "steps followed" look-for written on the class sheet; the model webs checked for range (families of every kind, a home language, a helper role) | Invented character first; a student may make up their own web; family and culture are never asked about by name in a check. Home languages and culture are welcome when offered, never asked about. SA4 is checked on the invented case only, never on a student's own conduct. The log and private web stay with the student. Agent reads: sensitivity (the agent first studies an education association's published guidance on families and cultures in the classroom). |
