n scene page (three clues and a checking question; the other side's reason; the snap-judgment check) and the care steps rehearsed from an unseen card, the teacher playing the one who struggles. Carry it out: "ask, don't guess" in group work. Family activity: retell a family story from another person's side, real or made up. Tools: the feelings faces chart, the shoes switch card, the care steps card, the gratitude wall, scene cards, the story partner page. Curio Class writes the scenes, the story partner page from its source, the cards and the page. Provisional cost for 30: about $10 printing. Begun here, owned in grade 5 (the band's owner year; the grade 5 unit that owns each is in the Seams table): CASEL.Relationship Skills.3, CASEL.Self-Awareness.6, CASEL.Social Awareness.1, CASEL.Social Awareness.3, CASEL.Social Awareness.4, CASEL.Social Awareness.5, CASEL.Social Awareness.8. | After unit 1 because reading others uses its strength scale and the snap-judgment check uses its stop-think-choose; after unit 2 because a student reads others after naming their own groups. Seven sub-skills, so three groups and 11 sessions. ELA grade 3 unit 3 (point of view, course days 81 to 119) comes after; social studies grade 3 unit 2 (rules and rights, course days 25 to 48) comes before (Cross-subject). Sessions 22 to 32 of the year, weeks 11 to 16. | Candidate: the teacher-acted scenes scripted in the unit plan; the story partner's game way taken from a source the sensitivity agent has read, not one of PE's or arts' grades 3 to 5 picks | SA6 on invented cases, the wrong guess resting on a neutral trait (quiet, new), never on skin, hair, dress, faith or accent; never blame of a group. RS3: no student is asked to explain their own culture; the partner's way is one invented child's, from a cited source. If a student tells of harm or risk in a care scene, health's steps. Agent reads: sensitivity (the agent first studies the source for the partner's way). |
