ented record; which goal to drop and why) and the focus plan's try-again step rehearsed from an unseen card. The course never records a student's own answer to SA7 or SA9. Carry it out: the weekly goal check. Family activity: plan one family job backward from its deadline. Tools: the goal steps card, the backward planner, the practice record, the focus plan card, the private log. Curio Class writes the planner, the records and cases and the page. Provisional cost for 30: about $10 printing. | After unit 13 because steady feelings come before long goals; its five weeks hold the four-week goal (the progression's pace note). Six sub-skills in two groups of three, each with two Fluency sessions, so 10 sessions. Health grade 5 unit 15 (weeks 1 to 4) starts its goal log first; ELA grade 5 unit 2 (course days 42 to 80) runs its research beside it (Cross-subject). Sessions 11 to 20 of the year, weeks 6 to 10. | Candidate: the class project's backward plan sized so its slip and recovery fall inside the unit | Growth is practice, strategy and help, never belief alone. SA7 plans are a character's; SA9 decisions stay private. Agent reads: sensitivity. |
