# source: https://casel.org/fundamentals-of-sel/what-is-the-casel-framework/
# version: CASEL 5 framework (CASEL "What Is the CASEL Framework?" page, current as fetched)
# fetched: 2026-10-27
# level: one CASEL sub-skill ("Such as:" item) within a competency, CASEL.<Competency>.<n>
# note: CASEL publishes no numbering for sub-skills; <n> is the order on the CASEL page (ours, not official). The page frames them as examples ("Such as"), not an exhaustive list.
# note: 40 sub-skills: Self-Awareness 9, Self-Management 7, Social Awareness 8, Responsible Decision-Making 7, Relationship Skills 9. Competency names spelled as in modules.csv.
# note: 2026-11-16: each line is now `CASEL.<Competency>.<n><TAB>our own words` (the shape of ma-hss-2018.txt), so a scope and sequence can be planned from this file. The words are ours, written for planning, never the publisher's.
# reuse: casel.org terms of use (read 2026-11-16) allow personal, non-commercial use only and bar copying or adapting without written permission; the page is marked all rights reserved. So ids and our own words only, never CASEL's sentences in any Curio Class page. Plan: docs/courses/sel/STANDARD.md.
# check: scripts/standards.py reads this file as an id list (valid as listed); the five competency codes in data/modules.csv remain valid.
CASEL.Self-Awareness.1	Understand who you are by bringing together the personal parts of yourself and the groups you belong to (family, culture, interests, roles)
CASEL.Self-Awareness.2	Name the strengths you bring, including those that come from your culture and the languages you speak
CASEL.Self-Awareness.3	Notice and name what you are feeling
CASEL.Self-Awareness.4	Tell the truth and act on your values, also when it is hard
CASEL.Self-Awareness.5	See how your feelings, what you care about and what you think shape one another
CASEL.Self-Awareness.6	Notice your own snap judgements and unfair assumptions about people, and question them
CASEL.Self-Awareness.7	Believe you can do a task, and act on that belief
CASEL.Self-Awareness.8	Treat skill and ability as things that grow with effort, practice and help
CASEL.Self-Awareness.9	Find what interests you and what gives your effort a purpose
CASEL.Self-Management.1	Handle strong feelings so they guide what you do rather than drive it
CASEL.Self-Management.2	Know and use ways to calm down and cope with stress
CASEL.Self-Management.3	Keep yourself on task and push yourself without being made to
CASEL.Self-Management.4	Pick targets you want to reach, alone or with others, and keep working at them
CASEL.Self-Management.5	Plan steps, manage time and keep materials in order
CASEL.Self-Management.6	Step forward and start something without waiting to be asked
CASEL.Self-Management.7	Act to shape your own life and your group's, alone and together
CASEL.Social Awareness.1	Take the point of view of another person
CASEL.Social Awareness.2	Notice what other people do well
CASEL.Social Awareness.3	Feel with others and act with care when they struggle
CASEL.Social Awareness.4	Pay attention to how others feel, and care about it
CASEL.Social Awareness.5	Notice what you are thankful for, and say so
CASEL.Social Awareness.6	Notice that places and groups have different unwritten rules, and that some of those rules were not fair
CASEL.Social Awareness.7	Read what a situation asks of you and the chances it offers
CASEL.Social Awareness.8	Understand how groups and systems (a school, the media, a government) shape how people act
CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.1	Ask questions and stay open to new ideas
CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.2	Choose after checking what the facts and numbers say
CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.3	Find solutions to problems in your own life and in your community
CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.4	Think ahead about what your actions may cause, and judge the results
CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.5	See that careful thinking helps in school and out of it
CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.6	Think about what you do for your own well-being and for the people close to you and around you
CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.7	Weigh who is affected by a choice, near and far, and what rules or groups it touches
CASEL.Relationship Skills.1	Speak and listen so that meaning gets across
CASEL.Relationship Skills.2	Build and keep healthy friendships and other relationships
CASEL.Relationship Skills.3	Work and get along well with people whose cultures differ from yours
CASEL.Relationship Skills.4	Work as a team and solve problems together
CASEL.Relationship Skills.5	Settle disagreements in ways that are calm and fair
CASEL.Relationship Skills.6	Say no to pressure to do something wrong or harmful
CASEL.Relationship Skills.7	Lead a group well, and know when to follow
CASEL.Relationship Skills.8	Ask for help when you need it, and offer help when others do
CASEL.Relationship Skills.9	Stand up for someone who is being treated unfairly


