122: {'strand': 'sa', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-sa-name-feelings', 'standard': '~CASEL.Self-Awareness.3', 'assumes': 'g2-sa-name-feelings', 'hands_on': 'g4-sa-name-feelings', 'model_in': 'feelings faces', 'model_out': 'feelings faces', 'words': 'frustrated; embarrassed; strength of a feeling; body clue', 'cross_subject': 'health:g3-meh-feelings-say (health has students say feelings in health topics with the same words)', 'notes': 'Unit 1, Think, feel, do. The feelings faces chart gains a 1 to 5 strength scale, and the student uses a three-step routine, "spot the body clue, name it, rate it", on characters in school-day scene cards (a lost recess game, a hard spelling quiz), and says why naming a feeling first makes it easier to handle. Across the band line: grade 2 named hidden and mixed feelings; grade 3 adds how strong and a named routine. Teacher note: checks name a character\'s feeling and its clue; no clinical words; a student\'s own feeling is never recorded.'}
123: {'strand': 'sa', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-sa-feel-think-link', 'standard': '~CASEL.Self-Awareness.5', 'assumes': 'g2-sa-feel-think-link', 'hands_on': 'g4-sa-feel-think-link', 'model_in': 'feelings faces', 'model_out': 'feelings faces', 'words': 'thought; feeling; action; chain; kinder thought', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 1, Think, feel, do. The student fills a think-feel-do chain for a scene-card character (a classmate did not wave back) and then uses "catch the thought, test it, try another": writes a second thought that fits the facts and shows how the feeling and action change. Grade 2 saw that the chain can change; grade 3 has the student change it, with a reason (thoughts are guesses, and guesses can be checked). Teacher note: a thinking skill used on characters, not a treatment; no student is asked to test their own thoughts aloud.'}
124: {'strand': 'sm', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-sm-big-feelings', 'standard': '~CASEL.Self-Management.1', 'assumes': 'g2-sm-big-feelings', 'hands_on': 'g4-sm-big-feelings', 'model_in': 'feelings faces; calm-down steps', 'model_out': 'feelings faces; calm-down steps', 'words': 'react; respond; pause; trigger', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Unit 1, Think, feel, do. The calm-down steps grow to four for grades 3 to 5: stop, breathe, name it, choose. The student rehearses them as a routine before acting on a big feeling in a school-day case (a teammate grabs the ball), then explains in a sentence the difference between reacting and responding. From grade 2's steps used once under a push to a routine the class names and gives a reason for."}
125: {'strand': 'sm', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-sm-calm-down', 'standard': '~CASEL.Self-Management.2', 'assumes': 'g2-sm-calm-down', 'hands_on': 'g4-sm-calm-down', 'model_in': 'calm-down steps', 'model_out': 'calm-down steps', 'words': 'breathe; stretch; count; cope; plan card', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 1, Think, feel, do. The student builds a plan card with the four calm-down steps and a menu of three body tools (slow breaths, a stretch, counting back from ten) for two school moments (before a test, after a recess argument), rehearses it daily for a week (kept between sessions as the unit\'s carry-out cue) and says why each step helps the body. Bigger than grade 2\'s two-step plan: four steps, each with its reason. Teacher note: breathing, stretching and pausing as plain body skills, with no spiritual framing; mental health topics are health\'s. Teacher note: if a student tells of harm or risk, follow health\'s steps (docs/courses/health/APPROACH.md, "If a student tells you something"): the school\'s reporting route and the counselor.'}
126: {'strand': 'rds', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-rds-careful-thinking', 'standard': '~CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.5', 'assumes': 'g2-rds-careful-thinking', 'hands_on': 'g4-rds-careful-thinking', 'model_in': 'stop-think-choose', 'model_out': 'stop-think-choose', 'words': 'rush; careful; check; result', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 1, Think, feel, do. Stop-think-choose grows to four steps for grades 3 to 5: stop, list two or three choices, think what each would cause, choose and check. The student compares two invented classmates doing the same school task, one who rushed and one who used the steps, and writes one place at home where the steps would help too. The K to 2 owner year said how thinking helped one project; now two cases sit side by side.'}
127: {'strand': 'rds', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-rds-good-for-us', 'standard': '~CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.6', 'assumes': 'g2-rds-good-for-us', 'hands_on': 'g4-rds-good-for-us', 'model_in': 'stop-think-choose', 'model_out': 'stop-think-choose', 'words': 'well-being; healthy; option; others', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 1, Think, feel, do. The student uses stop-think-choose on a school-day choice (finish a game indoors, or go out and play with a classmate who is alone) and lists what each option does for their own well-being and for the people around them, then picks with a reason. A step past grade 2: two options weighed, not one choice explained.'}
128: {'strand': 'sa', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-sa-who-i-am', 'standard': '~CASEL.Self-Awareness.1', 'assumes': 'g2-sa-who-i-am', 'hands_on': 'g4-sa-who-i-am', 'model_in': '', 'model_out': '', 'words': 'identity; group; role; belong', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 2, Who I am and what I bring. The student builds an identity web for an invented character (a team, a helper role at home, a club, a language) in three steps: list the groups, say what each adds, say where each part shows. They may make their own private web. Grade 2 showed one character in two groups; grade 3 builds a whole web and says why knowing it helps. Teacher note: invented character first; a student may make up their own; family and culture are never asked about by name in a check.'}
129: {'strand': 'sa', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-sa-my-strengths', 'standard': '~CASEL.Self-Awareness.2', 'assumes': 'g2-sa-my-strengths', 'hands_on': 'g4-sa-my-strengths', 'model_in': '', 'model_out': '', 'words': 'strength; skill; talent; evidence', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 2, Who I am and what I bring. A strengths hunt in three steps: recall a task that went well, name the skill it used, find another place it helps. Done first for a story character, then for the student if they choose, and a language spoken counts as a strength. The new demand over grade 2: each strength is backed by an example. Teacher note: home languages and culture are welcome when offered, never asked about.'}
130: {'strand': 'sa', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-sa-tell-truth', 'standard': '~CASEL.Self-Awareness.4', 'assumes': 'g2-sa-tell-truth', 'hands_on': 'g4-sa-tell-truth', 'model_in': 'stop-think-choose', 'model_out': 'stop-think-choose', 'words': 'honest; integrity; value; tempted', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Unit 2, Who I am and what I bring. On a school-day case (a classmate's answer sheet left in view), the student uses stop-think-choose to pick the honest action, names the value behind it, and says what honesty cost the character and what it kept. Grade 2 chose truth with a cost; grade 3 ties the choice to a named value. Checked on the invented case only, never on a student's own conduct."}
131: {'strand': 'sa', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-sa-what-interests-me', 'standard': '~CASEL.Self-Awareness.9', 'assumes': 'g2-sa-what-interests-me', 'hands_on': 'g4-sa-what-interests-me', 'model_in': '', 'model_out': '', 'words': 'interest; curious; purpose; explore', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Unit 2, Who I am and what I bring. The student keeps a private interest log for two weeks (kept between sessions as the unit's carry-out cue) (what they chose to do in free time, and why), then picks one entry and names a purpose for it (to help someone, to make something). The step from grade 2: the interest comes from what they actually did, not a single pick. Teacher note: the log stays with the student; it is checked only that the steps were followed, never for its content."}
132: {'strand': 'soc', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-soc-notice-good', 'standard': '~CASEL.Social Awareness.2', 'assumes': 'g2-soc-notice-good', 'hands_on': 'g4-soc-notice-good', 'model_in': '', 'model_out': '', 'words': 'specific; shout-out; feedback; effort', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 2, Who I am and what I bring. After a planned partner task the student gives a three-part shout-out (what they did, how they did it, why it mattered) and rewrites a vague "good job" into a specific one. Grade 2 named what and gave an example; grade 3 adds the how and the why.'}
133: {'strand': 'soc', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-soc-their-view', 'standard': '~CASEL.Social Awareness.1', 'assumes': 'g2-soc-their-view', 'hands_on': 'g4-soc-their-view', 'model_in': '', 'model_out': '', 'words': 'perspective; point of view; reason; side', 'cross_subject': "ela:e3-point-of-view (telling one's own view apart from a character's, the same move in reading)", 'notes': 'Unit 3, Walking in their shoes. The student uses a "shoes switch" on a school-day scene card: name what each person saw, what each wants and why each acted, then retell the scene from the other side. Grade 2 told both sides of a quarrel; grade 3 asks for the reason behind each side.'}
134: {'strand': 'soc', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-soc-care-when-struggle', 'standard': '~CASEL.Social Awareness.3', 'assumes': 'g2-soc-care-when-struggle', 'hands_on': 'g4-soc-care-when-struggle', 'model_in': 'feelings faces', 'model_out': 'feelings faces', 'words': 'empathy; comfort; ask; act', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 3, Walking in their shoes. Three care steps, "notice, ask what would help, do it", acted with a partner on a scene card where a character struggles (a lost library book, a hard reading turn); the student explains why asking first beats guessing. Up from grade 2: asking what the other person wants is now its own step, read from the feelings faces. Teacher note: if a student tells of harm or risk, follow health\'s steps (docs/courses/health/APPROACH.md, "If a student tells you something"): the school\'s reporting route and the counselor.'}
135: {'strand': 'soc', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-soc-read-feelings', 'standard': '~CASEL.Social Awareness.4', 'assumes': 'g2-soc-read-feelings', 'hands_on': 'g4-soc-read-feelings', 'model_in': 'feelings faces', 'model_out': 'feelings faces', 'words': 'body language; tone of voice; clue; check in', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Unit 3, Walking in their shoes. The student reads three kinds of clue (face, body, voice) in short teacher-acted school scenes, rates the strength on the feelings faces scale, and checks the guess with a question. Building on grade 2's hidden feelings, the guess now has a strength and a check."}
136: {'strand': 'soc', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-soc-thankful', 'standard': '~CASEL.Social Awareness.5', 'assumes': 'g2-soc-thankful', 'hands_on': 'g4-soc-thankful', 'model_in': '', 'model_out': '', 'words': 'gratitude; notice; express', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Unit 3, Walking in their shoes. The class keeps a gratitude wall for two weeks (kept between sessions as the unit's carry-out cue); each note names the act, the person and the difference it made, and the student says why noticing good things changes a class. Grade 2 thanked a helper once; grade 3 turns thanks into a habit kept over weeks."}
137: {'strand': 'sa', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-sa-snap-judgments', 'standard': '~CASEL.Self-Awareness.6', 'assumes': 'g2-sa-snap-judgments', 'hands_on': 'g4-sa-snap-judgments', 'model_in': 'stop-think-choose', 'model_out': 'stop-think-choose', 'words': 'assume; judgment; evidence; first thought', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Unit 3, Walking in their shoes. A three-step check on a snap judgment in a school-day case (a quiet new student called stuck-up): catch the first thought, ask what I actually know, find out before deciding, using stop-think-choose. Grade 2 caught and checked a guess; grade 3 names the steps and says why first guesses mislead. Teacher note: invented cases only; the skill is noticing and checking one's own guesses, never blame of a group."}
138: {'strand': 'rel', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-rel-different-ways', 'standard': '~CASEL.Relationship Skills.3', 'assumes': 'g2-rel-different-ways', 'hands_on': 'g4-rel-different-ways', 'model_in': '', 'model_out': '', 'words': 'culture; custom; respect; curious', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 3, Walking in their shoes. With a story partner from another place on a shared task, the student uses three steps: notice a different way, ask about it with respect, try it or combine it. The new piece after grade 2 is the respectful question. Teacher note: no student is asked to explain their own culture; customs come from stories and invented partners.'}
139: {'strand': 'soc', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-soc-why-rules', 'standard': '~CASEL.Social Awareness.8', 'assumes': 'g2-soc-why-rules', 'hands_on': 'g4-soc-why-rules', 'model_in': '', 'model_out': '', 'words': 'rule; system; school; community', 'cross_subject': 'social-studies:ss3-rules-rights (social studies traces a rule back to the problem it solves, SEL how the rule shapes what people do)', 'notes': 'Unit 3, Walking in their shoes. The student follows one school system (the lunch line, the bus line-up) in three steps: name the rule, say what it makes people do, say what would happen without it. Grade 2 sorted rules of class, school and town; grade 3 follows one system all the way through.'}
140: {'strand': 'rel', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-rel-talk-listen', 'standard': '~CASEL.Relationship Skills.1', 'assumes': 'g2-rel-talk-listen', 'hands_on': 'g4-rel-talk-listen', 'model_in': 'talk turn card', 'model_out': 'talk turn card', 'words': 'say back; build on; clarify; respond', 'cross_subject': 'ela:e3-discussion (the same class talk norms and words)', 'notes': 'Unit 4, When friends disagree. The talk turn card grows to four steps for grades 3 to 5: listen, say back what you heard, ask a question, add your idea. The student uses it in a planned partner talk on a friend-disagreement case and gives the reason for saying back first (the other person knows they were heard). Grade 2 asked and added; saying back and listening as a named step are new.'}
141: {'strand': 'rel', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-rel-friendships', 'standard': '~CASEL.Relationship Skills.2', 'assumes': 'g2-rel-friendships', 'hands_on': 'g4-rel-friendships', 'model_in': 'I-statement frame', 'model_out': 'I-statement frame', 'words': 'trust; respect; repair; healthy', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 4, When friends disagree. The student sorts friendship actions into "builds trust" and "breaks trust", then repairs a broken-trust moment from a scene card in three steps: own it, say sorry with the I-statement frame, make a plan to fix it. The student then rehearses the repair talk with a partner playing the friend who was hurt, saying the sorry with the I-statement frame. Grade 2 fixed one hurt; grade 3 adds a plan. Teacher note: no real friends are named.'}
142: {'strand': 'rel', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-rel-settle-disagreements', 'standard': '~CASEL.Relationship Skills.5', 'assumes': 'g2-rel-settle-disagreements', 'hands_on': 'g4-rel-settle-disagreements', 'model_in': 'talk turn card; I-statement frame', 'model_out': 'talk turn card; I-statement frame', 'words': 'compromise; calm; fair; solution', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 4, When friends disagree. The I-statement frame grows to four parts for grades 3 to 5: I feel, when, because, I need. With a partner, the student works an invented recess disagreement through "cool, talk, choose": calm first, both say an I-statement, then pick a fair solution from at least two. Grade 2 agreed one end; grade 3 compares two. The teacher plays any upset part.'}
143: {'strand': 'rel', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-rel-ask-offer-help', 'standard': '~CASEL.Relationship Skills.8', 'assumes': 'g2-rel-ask-offer-help', 'hands_on': 'g4-rel-ask-offer-help', 'model_in': 'problem size meter', 'model_out': 'problem size meter', 'words': 'trusted adult; help; offer; problem size', 'cross_subject': 'health:g3-s-which-helper (health names which helper fits which safety problem)', 'notes': 'Unit 4, When friends disagree. The problem size meter gains a fourth level for grades 3 to 5 (tiny, small, medium, big), each with who to go to. The student sizes school-day problems from a card deck, rehearses asking a trusted adult about a big one in three steps (go to them, say what happened, say what you need) with a partner playing the adult, and rehearses offering help on a small one aloud, the partner now playing the classmate. Grade 2 decided when a problem is too big; grade 3 rehearses the asking itself. Teacher note: if a student tells of harm or risk, follow health\'s steps (docs/courses/health/APPROACH.md, "If a student tells you something"): the school\'s reporting route and the counselor.'}
144: {'strand': 'soc', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-soc-read-situation', 'standard': '~CASEL.Social Awareness.7', 'assumes': 'g2-soc-read-situation', 'hands_on': 'g4-soc-read-situation', 'model_in': '', 'model_out': '', 'words': 'situation; expect; fit; chance', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 4, When friends disagree. The student reads a school situation with three questions (where am I, what does this place expect, what chance does it give me) on cases like the start of a group project or a fire drill, and acts the fitting response. Grade 2 named one chance on an invented case; grade 3 asks for it with a named question on school cases.'}
145: {'strand': 'rel', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-rel-lead-follow', 'standard': '~CASEL.Relationship Skills.7', 'assumes': 'g2-rel-lead-follow', 'hands_on': 'g4-rel-lead-follow', 'model_in': 'talk turn card', 'model_out': 'talk turn card', 'words': 'leader; follower; sum up; choose', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Unit 4, When friends disagree. In a small-group disagreement case the student leads with three steps (hear every idea with the talk turn card, sum up, help the group choose), then follows another leader's choice. Grade 2 gave everyone a turn; grade 3 leads the group to a choice."}
146: {'strand': 'rel', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-rel-say-no', 'standard': '~CASEL.Relationship Skills.6', 'assumes': 'g2-rel-say-no', 'hands_on': 'g4-rel-say-no', 'model_in': 'stop-think-choose; I-statement frame', 'model_out': 'stop-think-choose; I-statement frame', 'words': 'refuse; pressure; reason; walk away', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 5, Saying no, choosing well. A four-step refusal, "stop and think, say no clearly, give a reason, offer something else or walk away", rehearsed when a card character urges a school-day rule break (copying homework, sneaking into the closed gym); the student says why a reason makes a no stronger. Grade 2 held a no under a second push; grade 3 adds thinking before answering. Teacher note: the teacher or a card plays the pressure; no student plays the one who pushes; substance and body-safety topics are health\'s.'}
147: {'strand': 'rel', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-rel-stand-up', 'standard': '~CASEL.Relationship Skills.9', 'assumes': 'g2-rel-stand-up', 'hands_on': 'g4-rel-stand-up', 'model_in': 'I-statement frame', 'model_out': 'I-statement frame', 'words': 'upstander; speak up; include; report', 'cross_subject': 'health:g3-v-bullying (health teaches what bullying is, SEL rehearses the upstander steps)', 'notes': 'Unit 5, Saying no, choosing well. The student learns an upstander plan with four options (speak up with an I-statement, stand with the one left out, get help, check in after) and picks which fits each of two school cases of teasing or exclusion, with a reason. The student then rehearses the chosen words with a partner, using the I-statement frame, while the teacher or a card plays the unkind act. Up from grade 2: choosing among options. Teacher note: no student plays the unkind part or the one treated unfairly; school life only, and no cause is chosen by the course.'}
148: {'strand': 'rds', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-rds-ask-questions', 'standard': '~CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.1', 'assumes': 'g2-rds-ask-questions', 'hands_on': 'g4-rds-ask-questions', 'model_in': 'stop-think-choose', 'model_out': 'stop-think-choose', 'words': 'question; curious; open-minded; what if', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 5, Saying no, choosing well. Before a class choice the student asks three kinds of question (what, why, what if) of a scene-card case and changes their first idea when a new fact comes in, saying what changed their mind. Grade 2 asked and changed an idea; grade 3 names the kinds of question.'}
149: {'strand': 'rds', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-rds-check-facts', 'standard': '~CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.2', 'assumes': 'g2-rds-check-facts', 'hands_on': 'g4-rds-check-facts', 'model_in': 'stop-think-choose', 'model_out': 'stop-think-choose', 'words': 'fact; opinion; data; scaled graph', 'cross_subject': 'math:m3-scaled-graphs (reading a scaled bar graph of class data)', 'notes': 'Unit 5, Saying no, choosing well. The class makes a scaled bar graph of a survey (which game for indoor recess) and the student chooses from it, saying which fact decided and which opinion did not. Grade 2 read a picture graph; grade 3 reads a scaled one and pulls fact apart from opinion.'}
150: {'strand': 'rds', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-rds-solve-problems', 'standard': '~CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.3', 'assumes': 'g2-rds-solve-problems', 'hands_on': 'g4-rds-solve-problems', 'model_in': 'stop-think-choose; problem size meter', 'model_out': 'stop-think-choose; problem size meter', 'words': 'problem; brainstorm; solution; test', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Unit 5, Saying no, choosing well. The student solves a classroom problem (crowded coat hooks) in four steps: size it, list ideas, choose one, test it for a week and check (the test kept between sessions as the unit's carry-out cue). The grade 2 owner row picked a solution; grade 3 tests it."}
151: {'strand': 'rds', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-rds-think-ahead', 'standard': '~CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.4', 'assumes': 'g2-rds-think-ahead', 'hands_on': 'g4-rds-think-ahead', 'model_in': 'stop-think-choose', 'model_out': 'stop-think-choose', 'words': 'predict; result; later; judge', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 5, Saying no, choosing well. On a school-day choice card the student uses stop-think-choose to predict what each of two choices causes next, later that day and next week, and judges the result after. Grade 2 judged one result; grade 3 looks along time.'}
152: {'strand': 'soc', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-soc-fair-rules', 'standard': '~CASEL.Social Awareness.6', 'assumes': 'g2-soc-fair-rules', 'hands_on': 'g4-soc-fair-rules', 'model_in': '', 'model_out': '', 'words': 'fair; unfair; include; exclude', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 5, Saying no, choosing well. The student checks an invented game or club rule (only kids who own a ball may play) with three fairness questions (who can join, who is left out, how could it change) and rewrites it. Grade 2 rewrote one unfair rule; grade 3 has a named check to use on any rule. Teacher note: rules in a class, club or game on invented cases; unfair rules of the past wait for grade 5 by the grade table; no current dispute.'}
153: {'strand': 'rds', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-rds-who-is-affected', 'standard': '~CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.7', 'assumes': 'g2-rds-who-is-affected', 'hands_on': 'g4-rds-who-is-affected', 'model_in': 'stop-think-choose', 'model_out': 'stop-think-choose', 'words': 'affect; ring; school; rule', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 5, Saying no, choosing well. The student places who a class choice affects on a three-ring "who does it touch?" circle (me, my class, the school), with a reason for each, and names one school rule the choice must follow. Grade 2 named near and far; grade 3 places each person with a reason.'}
154: {'strand': 'sa', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-sa-i-can-try', 'standard': '~CASEL.Self-Awareness.7', 'assumes': 'g2-sa-i-can-try', 'hands_on': 'g4-sa-i-can-try', 'model_in': 'goal steps', 'model_out': 'goal steps', 'words': 'stretch goal; block; helper; if-then', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 6, Goals that stretch me. The student plans a stretch goal for an invented character on the goal steps card (goal, steps, a likely block, a helper) and writes an "if this happens, then I will" plan for the block. Grade 2 planned a try-again step after a setback; grade 3 names the block before it happens. The course never records a student\'s own answer.'}
155: {'strand': 'sa', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-sa-skills-grow', 'standard': '~CASEL.Self-Awareness.8', 'assumes': 'g2-sa-skills-grow', 'hands_on': 'g4-sa-skills-grow', 'model_in': '', 'model_out': '', 'words': 'practice; feedback; improve; strategy', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Unit 6, Goals that stretch me. The student keeps a three-week practice record (kept between sessions as the unit's carry-out cue) of one school skill (multiplication facts, a cartwheel), notes which practice or help made the biggest change, and explains growth as practice, strategy and help, never belief alone. Over grade 2: comparing which kind of practice helped most."}
156: {'strand': 'sm', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-sm-stay-on-task', 'standard': '~CASEL.Self-Management.3', 'assumes': 'g2-sm-stay-on-task', 'hands_on': 'g4-sm-stay-on-task', 'model_in': 'goal steps', 'model_out': 'goal steps', 'words': 'focus; distraction; self-talk; finish', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 6, Goals that stretch me. A three-step focus plan (spot the distraction, say the cue, move seats or ask) used in a planned work time and checked off on the goal steps card, with a try-again step for when the work itself gets hard (try another way, then ask). Grade 2 used one self-talk cue; grade 3 plans for the distraction ahead of time.'}
157: {'strand': 'sm', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-sm-set-goal', 'standard': '~CASEL.Self-Management.4', 'assumes': 'g2-sm-set-goal', 'hands_on': 'g4-sm-set-goal', 'model_in': 'goal steps', 'model_out': 'goal steps', 'words': 'goal; steps; block; check', 'cross_subject': 'health:g3-phw-set-goal (health applies goal setting to a health habit)', 'notes': "Unit 6, Goals that stretch me. The goal steps card grows to four steps for grades 3 to 5: goal, steps, block and plan, check. The student sets a three-week school goal (finish a chapter book), checks weekly and changes one step; the goal is kept between sessions as the unit's carry-out cue. The new demand over grade 2: a block is planned for before it comes."}
158: {'strand': 'sm', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-sm-plan-and-tidy', 'standard': '~CASEL.Self-Management.5', 'assumes': 'g2-sm-plan-and-tidy', 'hands_on': 'g4-sm-plan-and-tidy', 'model_in': 'goal steps', 'model_out': 'goal steps', 'words': 'schedule; deadline; organize; checklist', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 6, Goals that stretch me. The student plans a one-week class project on a planner with days and times, keeps a materials checklist, and reviews at the end what went to plan. Grade 2 planned two days; grade 3 a week.'}
159: {'strand': 'sm', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-sm-step-forward', 'standard': '~CASEL.Self-Management.6', 'assumes': 'g2-sm-step-forward', 'hands_on': 'g4-sm-step-forward', 'model_in': 'goal steps', 'model_out': 'goal steps', 'words': 'notice; start; first step; need', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Unit 6, Goals that stretch me. The student notices a class need, plans the first step on the goal steps card and starts it without being asked (a welcome kit for new students). Grade 2 started a small idea; grade 3 plans before starting.'}
160: {'strand': 'sm', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'g3-sm-have-a-say', 'standard': '~CASEL.Self-Management.7', 'assumes': 'g2-sm-have-a-say', 'hands_on': 'g4-sm-have-a-say', 'model_in': '', 'model_out': '', 'words': 'propose; vote; reason; evidence', 'cross_subject': "social-studies:ss3-taking-part (social studies on how people take part in a democracy, SEL on the student's own voice in class)", 'notes': "Unit 6, Goals that stretch me. The class proposes and votes on one change to a class routine; the student gives a reason with evidence and helps carry it out for two weeks, kept between sessions as the unit's carry-out cue. Grade 2 gave a reason; grade 3 backs it with evidence."}
