220: g5-soc-read-feelings | CASEL.Social Awareness.4 | Unit 4, Friends through change. The student reads mixed clues from an invented friend who says they are fine but is pulling away, checks in, respects the answer, and names a trusted adult to tell if the worry stays. Owner year for 3 to 5: clues that contradict the words. Teacher note: if a student tells of harm or risk, follow health's steps (docs/courses/health/APPROACH.md, "If a student tells you something"): the school's reporting route and the counselor.
221: g5-rel-talk-listen | CASEL.Relationship Skills.1 | Unit 4, Friends through change. The student uses the full talk turn card in an invented hard conversation about a friendship changing (a friend joins a new group), where saying back costs patience. Owner year for 3 to 5: the full card held when saying back costs patience.
222: g5-rel-friendships | CASEL.Relationship Skills.2 | Unit 4, Friends through change. On two invented cases, a friend who will be in a different class next year and an invented friend who will only play if the student leaves another child out, the student plans how to keep the first friendship across the change and how to step back from the second with a trusted adult's help, using the I-statement frame. The student rehearses the opening of each talk with a partner playing the friend. Owner year for 3 to 5: a friendship kept through change, and stepped back from when it asks something unkind. Teacher note: no real friends are named; relationship health topics are health's. Teacher note: if a student tells of harm or risk, follow health's steps (docs/courses/health/APPROACH.md, "If a student tells you something"): the school's reporting route and the counselor.
223: g5-rel-settle-disagreements | CASEL.Relationship Skills.5 | Unit 4, Friends through change. With a partner, the student works a disagreement where any fair solution costs each side something, using the I-statement frame, and chooses a compromise both can keep. Owner year for 3 to 5: a compromise where each side gives something up. The teacher plays any upset part.
224: g5-rel-ask-offer-help | CASEL.Relationship Skills.8 | Unit 4, Friends through change. On an invented case the student sizes two problems on the problem size meter, then rehearses with a partner asking a teacher for help when asking feels costly (in front of friends), the partner playing the teacher, and offering help to an invented new classmate, the partner playing the newcomer. Owner year for 3 to 5: asking holds even when friends are watching. Teacher note: if a student tells of harm or risk, follow health's steps (docs/courses/health/APPROACH.md, "If a student tells you something"): the school's reporting route and the counselor.
225: g5-rel-say-no | CASEL.Relationship Skills.6 | Unit 4, Friends through change. The student rehearses the refusal steps against a card character who adds a social cost ("then you're not in our group"), holds the no and names another friend to turn to. Owner year for 3 to 5: the no held against a social cost. Teacher note: the teacher or a card plays the pressure; no student plays the one who pushes; substance and body-safety topics are health's.
226: g5-soc-notice-good | CASEL.Social Awareness.2 | Unit 5, My voice, our group. The student gives specific feedback to a teammate whose work was overlooked, even when the group praises someone else. Owner year for 3 to 5: credit given against the group's lean.
227: g5-soc-thankful | CASEL.Social Awareness.5 | Unit 5, My voice, our group. The student thanks someone who helped the group at a cost to themselves, naming what it cost. Owner year for 3 to 5: thanks for help that had a price, said in specific words.
228: g5-rel-different-ways | CASEL.Relationship Skills.3 | Unit 5, My voice, our group. The student works in a mixed team on the school improvement and resolves a clash of habits with respect, using the three steps. Owner year for 3 to 5: a clash of habits resolved on a real class project. Teacher note: no student is asked to explain their own culture; customs come from stories and invented partners.
229: g5-rel-lead-follow | CASEL.Relationship Skills.7 | Unit 5, My voice, our group. The student leads a group decision when the group is split, and follows well when their own idea loses. Owner year for 3 to 5: leading a split group, and following when one's own idea loses.
230: g5-rel-stand-up | CASEL.Relationship Skills.9 | Unit 5, My voice, our group. On an invented case (the student's own friend group laughs at a schoolmate's mistake at the class concert), the student chooses the safest upstander option, rehearses the chosen words with a partner using the I-statement frame while the teacher or a card plays the unkind act, and says why that option fits. Owner year for 3 to 5: speaking up when it may cost standing with friends. Teacher note: no student plays the unkind part or the one treated unfairly; school life only, and no cause is chosen by the course.
