1: # Independent frame review: Social and Emotional Learning, Grades K to 2
2: 
3: Date: 2026-11-25  
4: Course: `social-and-emotional-learning-grades-k-to-2`  
5: Read only. No files were changed.
6: 
7: ## Verdict
8: 
9: The frame has a sound instructional foundation: all 120 selected progression rows are placed exactly once, the three years differ in depth, and rehearsal, invented cases and family activities are built into every year. It needs revision before scope writing because its fall and spring checks replace the required mid-year and year-end checks, several owned standards remain partial, and the leave-out rule lacks a workable kindergarten fallback. The most important change is to settle a calendar that preserves complete annual teaching and genuine course-level checks.
10: 
11: **Eight findings:** three serious, three moderate and two minor.
12: 
13: ## What I read
14: 
15: - The frame-read brief and the after-core provisions of frame-write; EXPERT.md; the SEL lens; FOUNDATION.md; relevant APPROACH, PRODUCTION-PATH and BASELINE provisions.
16: - ADOPTION-BAR-SUBJECTS.md: shared requirements, part 9 and the SEL status row; SEL STANDARD.md and APPROACH.md.
17: - The complete course frame; its course-list selector, frames.csv entry and calendar.csv rows; CALENDAR.md.
18: - The 120 selected SEL progression rows, grade 3 receiving rows, sel-edges.md and the 40 standard statements.
19: - Relevant Units-table rows in the K to 2 ELA, mathematics and social studies frames; the health frame’s relevant units and cross-subject table; health’s disclosure instructions.
20: - Earlier SEL pre-work and progression reviews and their recorded fixes. Earlier frame reports were consulted for repeated finding types.
21: - Outside sources linked below.
22: 
23: Kindergarten has no preceding course. The grades 3 to 5 SEL frame does not yet exist, so the outgoing seam was checked against its progression rows.
