92: **Location:** Days and Carry it out bullets; Inside the band; units 4 and 5.
93: 
94: The frame relies on a “Given:” readiness item when a school leaves out an earlier unit. That does not supply the missing teaching or model. In kindergarten there is also no previous-year SEL row to fall back on.
95: 
96: For example, leaving out unit 2 removes the feelings chart needed by unit 4 and the calm-down routine required by unit 5. Leaving out unit 1 removes the talk routine used in later partner work. A check can reveal these gaps, but cannot make the later unit runnable.
97: 
98: **Exact fix:** Add a leave-out bridge table identifying each later unit’s required incoming model and its fallback.
99: 
100: At minimum:
101: 
102: - Unit 4 supplies and models the pictured feeling clues it needs when unit 2 was omitted.
103: - Unit 5 supplies and rehearses “stop, breathe” before disagreement work when unit 2 was omitted.
104: - Later partner units supply the two pictured talk steps when unit 1 was omitted.
105: - Each receiving unit places its bridge within a named Understanding session and states what practice it replaces.
106: - Kindergarten readiness wording distinguishes new teaching from retrieval. Later grades use an earlier taught row only when that row was actually taught.
107: 
108: Keep the omitted unit’s coverage disclaimer. A brief bridge does not establish full coverage of that unit’s standards.
109: 
110: ### 4. The three standards transferred from library remain outside the ownership record
111: 
112: **Severity:** Moderate  
113: **LAYER:** progression, frame  
114: **REPEAT:** yes, ownership and cross-subject coverage tracing recur in the earlier SEL reviews  
115: **Confidence:** firm
116: 
117: **Location:** Standard bullet, Library subsection and For the lead 4; the three grade 2 rows named below.
