43: 
44: ## Pattern notes for the other SEL frames
45: 
46: - Fit both course-level checks inside 64 sessions, after units 2 and 5 or wherever the core check weeks leave room, and say how the last unit is sampled.
47: - Budget the session minutes in the frame; cap new sub-skills per Understanding session to what the minutes hold.
48: - Owner-year rows must teach every part of the code (culture in RS3 and SA2, chance in SO7, values in SA5).
49: - Cite STANDARD section 7 "Shared steps" and the written health and PE frames' real units; never "being written".
50: - List leave-out bridges; name every unit's retrieval; cite game sources at frame time; pick a game the class does not know.
51: 
52: ## Left for the lead
53: 
54: 1. AASL ids: scripts/progression.py and scripts/frame.py accept AASL.V.D.1, V.D.2 and III.D.2 for SEL rows.
55: 2. Health K to 2: listening card opens with the talk turn card's steps; I-statement, refusal second push and goal rungs cite STANDARD section 7; health rows gain cross_subject leans to SEL.
56: 3. PE K to 2: Ampe repeats in grade 1 unit 14 (pick: PE swaps in another Ghanaian game); calm card picture in grade 1 unit 11; goal rungs in K unit 6 and grade 2 unit 16.
57: 4. Spanish family notes need a translation read brief.
58: 5. Band "k-2" is outside frame.py's K to 8 clash check; weeks placed by hand.
59: 6. DESK-ANSWERS log lines: shared steps, "I need" wording, leave-out bridge rule.
60: 7. ADOPTION-BAR-SUBJECTS SEL row's stale owed clause.
61: 8. After-core check clashes (SEL not moved):
62:    - Week 26, K, 1 and 2: SEL year-end check with visual arts' year-end check.
63:    - Week 27, grade 1: SEL respond with health's year-end check.
64:    - Week 27, grade 2: SEL respond with health's, PE's and English language development's year-end checks.
65:    - Week 11, grade 2: SEL respond with health's mid-year check.
66: 
67: ## For Cory
68: 
69: 1. **Unit sizes (scope).** q-fix-sel-1 set units of 11 and 10 (short path 5 and 6), which fills all 64 sessions and leaves none for the mid-year and year-end checks the 2026-11-25 rule requires. This frame uses 11 and 8 (kindergarten 12 and 8; short path 5 and 5, kindergarten 6 and 4, plus 2 for checks), freeing 4 sessions a year. Each group still gets Understanding, Fluency and Application. Alternatives: 68 sessions a year, or fold the checks into unit Check sessions (no separate check). Pick: accept for K to 2, and let each other band set its sizes from its minutes under the same rule.
70: 2. **Year-end check placement (scope).** Core check weeks fill weeks 28 to 32, so the year-end check sits after unit 5 (week 26) and unit 6 is sampled by its own assessment and next year's mid-year check. Options: (a) allow week 32, shared with core checks; (b) as now; (c) three sessions in some weeks. Pick: (b).
71: 3. **Supply ceiling (money).** About $55 to $60 a year printing plus about $21 once, for 30 children; no ceiling is set. Pick: set none until the first unit plans price it.

