291: ### After the core subjects
292: 
293: Every later subject runs by docs/COURSE-RUN.md from stage 1 (pre-work) on. The order below still stands.
294: 
295: First the 6 electives of the four core subjects (precalculus, statistics, calculus, earth and space science,
296: environmental science, psychology). Then the 49 courses of the other subjects (47 active plus the 2 shelved world
297: language courses): arts and music, health and PE, computer science, career and technical education, social and
298: emotional learning, English language development, and library and research skills; world languages stay shelved
299: (settled 2026-11-13, see DESK-ANSWERS). Personal finance is not a course of its own: Economics teaches it, lightly
300: integrated, and data/courses.csv does not flag it core (settled 2026-11-14, see DESK-ANSWERS). Where a core
301: progression leans on one of the later subjects (English language development with ELA; health with science), the
302: cross_subject column notes it for then.
303: 
304: **Before a new subject's scopes** (lead 2026-11-15, see DESK-ANSWERS). Every elective and every later subject passes
305: these before Codex writes its first scope:
306: 1. Its data layouts are gated before any writer runs: days.csv and source-map.csv in sequence-write.md's layout,
307:    checked by sequence.py, and the subject's progression checked. No writer invents a column.
308: 2. One pilot course per subject first (Codex write, both reads, fix), then the brief is frozen for the rest of that
309:    subject; only a finding that breaks a gate reopens it.
310: 3. The rule 2 readiness and retrieval count runs in the scope gate (sequence.py rule2_notes) on every course, so the
311:    gaps show at scope stage, not at the skeleton.
312: 4. The unit skeleton runs on the pilot course before the others are written, so its adapter needs are known early.
313: 
314: ### People and a second reader, through all of it
315: 
316: - **A reader of a different model kind** at each baseline and in P5d's calibration: Codex reads cold against the
317:   same brief, by script with no clicks (scripts/codex_read.py), and its findings are compared with the expert's.
318:   Codex's weekly budget resets often and is open for large use; Pro ends 2026-11-30.
319: - **Reviewers are agents** (FOUNDATION 7.3). The expert agent, checked in P5, and Codex are the reviewers. The
320:   answer-key, safety and sensitivity agents do the content reads FOUNDATION 7.3 assigns, each cold and after
321:   studying its sources (docs/pipeline/briefs/sensitivity-read.md). No outside human reader is planned. Pilots are
322:   retired; the probe and guard replace them.
