100: | 3, 4 and 5 (one course each) | All six | Key words, searching a catalog and a chosen site, note-making, primary and secondary sources, a simple bibliography, first lateral checks of a site |
101: | Grades 6 to 8 (one course) | All six | Search strategy, lateral reading, judging evidence and who is behind it, paraphrase and quotation, citation in one style, fair use basics, checking text made by a machine like any other source (who made it, what it cites) |
102: | Grades 9 to 12 (one course) | All six | Research question design, databases, search operators and filters, and open sources, lateral reading on hard cases, synthesis across sources, full citation, copyright, licenses, fair use and asking a maker's permission (checked against the 9 to 12 band file, 2026-11-21), checking and disclosing the use of machine-made text, sharing a research product |
