FILE docs/courses/social-and-emotional-learning-grades-6-to-8/frame.md
12: - **Shared steps with health and PE.** The talk turn card, calm-down steps, I-statement frame, goal steps card and refusal options use the one set of words in STANDARD section 7 ("Shared steps"), so a student meets one card across SEL, health and PE. Where health or PE teaches a card first in a year, the SEL unit opens with it as retrieval where the school runs that course, and teaches it itself where it does not (Cross-subject, Health and PE).
13: - **Leave-out.** A school may leave out a unit (STANDARD section 5.6). Where a later unit uses a card the left-out unit made or grew, that unit's first Understanding session teaches the card's one-step form itself in its first ten minutes, in place of the retrieval opening and part of that session's rehearsal, and claims none of the left-out unit's sub-skills: the feelings scale with the exact word (unit 2; first needed by units 4, then 10, 15); the five-step calm-down steps and the five-step stop-think-choose (unit 3; units 4, 5, 6, then 8, 10, 15); the talk turn card's first step, choose how to talk, the refusal options and the I-statement (unit 4; units 6, 8, 11, 14, 17); the fairness questions and the who-is-affected map (unit 5; units 9, 12, 13, 16); the upstander options (unit 6; units 11, 18). Grade 6 units 1 and 2 use the grade 5 forms of the cards, which SEL 3 to 5 taught; the readiness check and the same ten-minute bridge cover a class that did not take it.
21: - **Tools and costs.** Kept all band: the talk turn card, feelings scale (the grade 5 feelings faces with their 1 to 5 strength), calm-down step card and tool menu, stop-think-choose card, goal steps card, problem size meter and I-statement frame (all from SEL 3 to 5, grown here in units 2, 3 and 4), plus the refusal options card, fairness questions card, who-is-affected map and upstander options card. Each unit names its tools, what Curio Class writes and a provisional cost for 30 students; printing runs about $8 to $10 a unit, about $55 to $60 a year, plus about $5 to $10 of project supplies in units 6, 12 and 18 and $4 once for a two-minute sand timer per group (unit 13). No supply ceiling is set for SEL (For the lead 10); these are planning figures, not quotes.
23: - **Disclosure.** Asking for help, stress, pressure, friendship, conflict and upstander units can bring a disclosure, and middle school cases (a worry that does not go away, a friend's secret, a mocked classmate) make one more likely. Every unit follows health's steps (docs/courses/health/APPROACH.md, "If a student tells you something"): the school's reporting route and the counselor. Health owns substances, body safety, sleep and mental health topics, self-harm and suicide; SEL never teaches them, and its cases never use them.
